  'The Air Force said that from the evening of 14 October Russia launched 2 Kh-59 missiles and 580 drones, 536 of which were downed or suppressed, with hits at 31 locations. Kirovohrad region was under attack for more than 10 hours: three killed and six injured in Kropyvnytskyi, with strikes on enterprises, logistics and homes; two were killed in Dnipropetrovsk region, 5 people hurt in Chortkiv, and two enterprises hit in Poltava region. Zelensky said Russia launched more than 850 Shaheds in a day and a half; Ukrenergo reported new outages in five regions.',
